{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MmuR9V9Closure","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MmuR9V9Closure","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder"],"declarations":34,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.universal_habiro_closure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.universal_habiro_closure","kind":"theorem","line":448,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L448-L487","doc":"**Theorem (formerly billed as conditional on the removed\n`UniversalHabiroStructure` class).**\n\nIf the universal Habiro structure holds at `q`, then both the m_μ\nR9+V9 closure and the Q_β c_3 3-rung closure represent genuine\ncategorical derivations of their respective L2 observables at `q`.\n\n**Corrected 2026-08-21** (vacuity ledger,\n`proof-no-unused-hypothesis-rfl`, verdict genuine).  This was billed as\n\"the §3b-cond conditional-class theorem: its conclusion is the L2\nclosure of both observables, conditional on the class instance.\"  It is\nnot, and never was:\n\n- both conjuncts are closed by `rfl`, so the statement is two\n  *definitional unfoldings* joined by `∧` — it says that\n  `m_mu_R9_V9` and `qbetaC3Closure` unfold to their own definitions;\n- neither `hq : 0 < q` nor the `[UniversalHabiroStructure q]` instance\n  was used, and the instance in particular was advertised as the\n  structure supplying the closure while contributing nothing.  Both\n  unused binders have been dropped, which is what makes the remaining\n  content honest: unfolding lemmas that do not pretend to be\n  conditional on an open structure.\n\nThe instance could not have contributed: `UniversalHabiroStructure`'s\ntwo fields are `markov_trace_origin : True` and\n`cinquefoil_framing_t25_origin : True`, both self-described opaque\nmarkers, so the class constrains nothing.\n\n**A universal Habiro closure is therefore NOT established here.**  It\nremains one of the framework's open targets (Theorems 4 + 5); the\nempirical position is unchanged — witnesses show the closures hold to\nwithin their L2 100× gates at proton-pinned q₀, the class instance has\nNOT been constructed, NEAR-MATCH tier, production wiring untouched. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qbetaC3Rung1_times_hbarQ_seven_eq_delta_V9","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qbetaC3Rung1_times_hbarQ_seven_eq_delta_V9","kind":"theorem","line":413,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L413-L425","doc":"**Theorem 20 (proved).** Cross-rung product identity for Q_β c_3.\n\nThe rung 1 (containing `habiroT25 q`) and the m_μ V9 rung\n(containing the same `habiroT25 q`) can be related directly:\n\n  `qbetaC3Rung1 q · hbarQ q^7 = delta_V9 q`\n\nA restatement of Theorem 6 (`delta_V9_eq_hbarQ_seven_times_qbetaC3Rung1`)\nin product form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.habiroTnSq_times_n_sq_eq_quantumInt_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.habiroTnSq_times_n_sq_eq_quantumInt_three","kind":"theorem","line":400,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L400-L411","doc":"**Theorem 19 (proved).** General framing-ladder normalisation:\nfor `n ≥ 1`, multiplying `habiroTnSq n q` by `n²` recovers `[3]_q`.\n\nThe n-parametric form of Theorem 18 — the framing factor *always*\nclears to `[3]_q` via the squared T(2,n) crossing index, for any\npositive lepton index. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.habiroT25_times_25_eq_quantumInt_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.habiroT25_times_25_eq_quantumInt_three","kind":"theorem","line":388,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L388-L398","doc":"**Theorem 18 (proved).** Clearing the `25` denominator from\n`habiroT25`: multiplying by 25 recovers the bare quantum integer.\n\n  `25 · T_{25}(q) = [3]_q`\n\nA direct cancellation identity used downstream when normalising\nclosure formulas. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hbarQ_pos_of_one_lt_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hbarQ_pos_of_one_lt_q","kind":"theorem","line":379,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L379-L386","doc":"**Theorem 17 (proved).** Substrate `ℏ_q` is strictly positive on\nthe physical regime `q > 1`. Foundational positivity lemma needed for\ndownstream sign-tracking in the closure formulas. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.delta_total_mmu_factored","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.delta_total_mmu_factored","kind":"theorem","line":366,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L366-L377","doc":"**Theorem 16 (proved).** The m_μ R9 + V9 total correction\nfactors as `delta_total_mmu q = hbarQ q^6 · (q/5 + hbarQ q² · [3]_q / 25)`.\n\nThis makes the R9-out-front factoring explicit: the V9 rung is the\nfirst-order categorical correction to the R9 leading rung. Connects to\nthe S11 factored Habiro form (`mmu_simpler_form_search_probe.py`):\n`δ_total = (ℏ_q^6 × q / 5) × (1 + ℏ_q² × [3]_q / 5)` modulo the q\nfactor on `[3]_q` (which makes S11 slightly less accurate than V9). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.habiroTnSq_five_seven_ratio_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.habiroTnSq_five_seven_ratio_identity","kind":"theorem","line":356,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L356-L364","doc":"**Theorem 15 (proved).** Cross-lepton framing ratio\nμ/τ, as the `n²`-normalisation `25·T(5) = 49·T(7)` (both sides equal\n`[3]_q`). Equivalently `habiroTnSq 7 q / habiroTnSq 5 q = 25/49 = (5/7)²`.\n\nA predicted ratio testable when m_τ Habiro analog is wired. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.habiroTnSq_three_five_ratio_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.habiroTnSq_three_five_ratio_identity","kind":"theorem","line":345,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L345-L354","doc":"**Theorem 14 (proved).** Cross-lepton framing ratio\ne/μ: `habiroTnSq 3 q × 25 = habiroTnSq 5 q × 9` for all q.\n\nStated as the `n²`-normalisation `9·T(3) = 25·T(5)` (both sides equal\n`[3]_q`). Equivalently the ratio `habiroTnSq 5 q / habiroTnSq 3 q =\n9/25 = (3/5)²` when the numerator `[3]_q` cancels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.habiroTnSq_at_q_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.habiroTnSq_at_q_one","kind":"theorem","line":328,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L328-L338","doc":"**Theorem 13 (proved).** The framing-ladder family at the\nclassical limit q = 1: `habiroTnSq n 1` is finite for n ≥ 1.\n\nThis follows because at q = 1, the quantumInt formula has indeterminate\n`0/0`, which Lean's field instance resolves to 0. (The categorical\nlimit `[3]_q → 3` as q → 1 holds via L'Hôpital; in Lean's pointwise\nalgebra, `quantumInt 3 1 = (1 - 1)/(1 - 1) = 0/0 = 0`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.habiroTnSq_seven_explicit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.habiroTnSq_seven_explicit","kind":"theorem","line":319,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L319-L326","doc":"**Theorem 12 (proved).** Tau framing factor at T(2,7) septafoil:\n`habiroTnSq 7 q = [3]_q / 49`. Cross-lepton testable prediction:\nif the universal Habiro structure derives from the T(2,n) framing,\nthen the tau analog of m_μ V9 should involve a `[3]_q / 49` factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.habiroTnSq_three_explicit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.habiroTnSq_three_explicit","kind":"theorem","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L312-L317","doc":"**Theorem 11 (proved).** Electron framing factor at T(2,3) trefoil:\n`habiroTnSq 3 q = [3]_q / 9`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.habiroT25_eq_habiroTnSq_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.habiroT25_eq_habiroTnSq_five","kind":"theorem","line":305,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L305-L310","doc":"**Theorem 10 (proved).** The empirical muon factor `habiroT25` is\nthe n=5 case of the general framing-ladder family. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.habiroTnSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.habiroTnSq","kind":"def","line":301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L301-L303","doc":"General lepton framing-ladder factor: `[3]_q / n²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qbetaC3Closure_at_q_one_equals_jonesHopfClassicalLimit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qbetaC3Closure_at_q_one_equals_jonesHopfClassicalLimit","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L265-L280","doc":"**Bridge theorem (proved).** At the classical limit q = 1, the\nempirical 3-rung Q_β c_3 closure equals the precision ladder's\n`jonesHopfClassicalLimit = -2`.\n\nDirect consequence of `qbetaC3Closure_at_q_one_equals_neg_two`\n(Theorem 8) and the definition `jonesHopfClassicalLimit := -2`\n(line 58 of QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean).\n\nThis is the formal Lean record of the empirical-vs-categorical\nconsistency at the classical limit: two different formulas\n(empirical 3-rung Habiro at q-dependent vs. q-independent J_Hopf\nconjecture) give the same value at q = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.mmu_closure_factor_at_q_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.mmu_closure_factor_at_q_one","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L247-L257","doc":"**Theorem 9 (proved).** Classical-limit consistency for m_μ: at\nq = 1, the R9+V9 corrected prediction reduces to the bare\n`m_e · vol_4_1 / hbarQ q²` formula evaluated at q = 1 (modulo the\nhbarQ singularity).\n\nSpecifically, `1 - delta_total_mmu 1 = 1`, so the closure factor\ncollapses to unity at the classical limit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qbetaC3Closure_at_q_one_equals_neg_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qbetaC3Closure_at_q_one_equals_neg_two","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L235-L245","doc":"**Theorem 8 (proved).** Classical-limit consistency: the empirical\n3-rung Q_β c_3 closure formula reduces to `J_Hopf(q=1) = -2` at q = 1.\n\nThis is a structural check — the empirical Habiro closure is consistent\nwith the (proven) categorical conjecture `c_3 → J_Hopf` at the\nclassical limit. Connects to `QbetaC3StructuralFormClass` in\n`QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder.lean` line 410. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.corrections_vanish_at_q_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.corrections_vanish_at_q_one","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L224-L233","doc":"**Theorem 7 (proved).** All categorical corrections vanish at the\nclassical limit `q = 1`.\n\nEach correction is proportional to `hbarQ 1 = (1-1)/1 = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.delta_V9_eq_hbarQ_seven_times_qbetaC3Rung1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.delta_V9_eq_hbarQ_seven_times_qbetaC3Rung1","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L214-L222","doc":"**Theorem 6 (proved).** Cross-observable jet-order identity:\nthe m_μ V9 correction is exactly ℏ_q⁷ times the Q_β c_3 rung 1.\n\nThis makes the **shared `habiroT25` factor** with **different jet\norders** explicit as a single identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.habiroT25_framing_family_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.habiroT25_framing_family_exists","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L183-L205","doc":"**Theorem 5 (proved, formal-existence form).**\n\nThe `1/n²` framing-ladder family is realised by\n`framing n r := [3]_r / (n : ℝ)²`:\n  - `framing 5 q = [3]_q / 25 = T_{25}(q) = habiroT25 q` (muon T(2,5))\n  - `framing n q = [3]_q / n²` for all n (cross-lepton testable)\n\n**Proven** via the explicit witness.\n\nThe DEEP CATEGORICAL CLAIM — that this family IS the T(2,n) cinquefoil\nframing factor at the substrate level, with the n=5 selection matching\nthe muon's torus-knot assignment from\n[`lepton_t2n_torus_tower.py`](../../../../../computations/lepton_t2n_torus_tower.py)\n— is conjectural. It is open (bean `qou-n2un`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hbar_q_jet_orders_family_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hbar_q_jet_orders_family_exists","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L159-L181","doc":"**Theorem 4 (proved, formal-existence form).**\n\nThe jet-order family appearing across both closures is realised by\nthe explicit function `f n r := ℏ_q r ^ n`:\n  - `f 6 q = ℏ_q⁶` (m_μ R9 ℏ_q⁶ factor, h³ jet)\n  - `f 8 q = ℏ_q⁸` (m_μ V9 ℏ_q⁸ factor, h⁴ jet)\n  - `f 3 q = ℏ_q³` (Q_β c_3 rung 2 ℏ_q³ factor)\n\n**Proven** via the explicit witness; the formal existence of a function\nrealising these jet indices is trivial.\n\nThe DEEP CATEGORICAL CLAIM — that this family IS the Markov-trace\nexpansion of a specific Wenzl-Hoefsmit operator (rather than a mere\nindexing function) — is conjectural and absent from the present Lean\ninfrastructure. It is open (bean `qou-n2un`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qbetaC3Base_unfold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qbetaC3Base_unfold","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L145-L157","doc":"**Theorem 3 (proved).** Unfold the Q_β c_3 base to its canonical\ndefinitional form `-(q² + q⁻¹²)`.\n\nThis is the **definitional unfolding** (proof is `rfl` after `unfold`),\nrecorded as a named identity so downstream files can reference the\ncanonical form directly without repeating the `unfold`. Identifies\n`qbetaC3Base` with the negative symmetric q²-block eigenvalue sum\n(which equals `-[2]_{q²}` where `[2]_x := x + x⁻¹`; this stronger\nfactorization is NOT proved here and would require `field_simp +\nring` over `q ≠ 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qbetaC3Rung1_factors_via_habiroT25","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qbetaC3Rung1_factors_via_habiroT25","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L132-L143","doc":"**Theorem 2 (proved).** The Q_β c_3 rung 1 factors through the\nSAME universal Habiro building block `T_{25}(q) = [3]_q / 25`:\n\n  `qbetaC3Rung1(q) = ℏ_q · T_{25}(q)`\n\nCombined with Theorem 1, this establishes that BOTH observables'\nclosures contain `T_{25}` as a factor — the empirical \"shared\nbuilding block\" finding made categorically explicit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.delta_V9_factors_via_habiroT25","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.delta_V9_factors_via_habiroT25","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L121-L130","doc":"**Theorem 1 (proved).** The m_μ V9 rung factors through the\nuniversal Habiro building block `T_{25}(q) = [3]_q / 25`:\n\n  `δ_V9(q) = ℏ_q⁸ · T_{25}(q)`\n\nThis makes the shared Habiro factor explicit in the m_μ closure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qbetaC3Closure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qbetaC3Closure","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L110-L112","doc":"Q_β c_3 3-rung closure prediction. Closes 2.65 ppm at proton-pinned q₀. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qbetaC3Rung2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qbetaC3Rung2","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L105-L108","doc":"Q_β c_3 second rung (T7 cleanest): `ℏ_q³ / [2]_q`. Pure quantum-\ninteger ratio, no empirical coefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qbetaC3Rung1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qbetaC3Rung1","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L101-L103","doc":"Q_β c_3 first rung: `ℏ_q · [3]_q / 25 = ℏ_q · T_{25}(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qbetaC3Base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qbetaC3Base","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L96-L99","doc":"Categorical base for Q_β c_3: `-(q² + q⁻²)`. Empirically identified\nin PR #1773's 15-candidate single-formula re-run as the best base\n(9,109 ppm without further correction). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.m_mu_R9_V9","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.m_mu_R9_V9","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L90-L92","doc":"m_μ prediction with R9 + V9 correction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.delta_total_mmu","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.delta_total_mmu","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L86-L88","doc":"Total m_μ categorical correction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.delta_V9","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.delta_V9","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L82-L84","doc":"m_μ V9 second-rung correction: `δ_V9 = ℏ_q⁸ · [3]_q / 25`. NEAR-MATCH form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.delta_R9","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.delta_R9","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L78-L80","doc":"m_μ R9 first-rung correction: `δ_R9 = ℏ_q⁶ · q / 5`. NEAR-MATCH form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.habiroT25","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.habiroT25","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L68-L74","doc":"**Universal Habiro building block** `T_{25}(q) = [3]_q / 25 = [3]_q / 5²`.\n\nEmpirically discovered in PR #1781 to appear in BOTH m_μ V9 (rung 2,\nh⁴ jet) and Q_β c_3 (rung 1, h¹ jet). The `5²` denominator parallels\nthe m_μ R9 `/5` denominator. Conjectural origin: T(2,5) cinquefoil\nframing factor of the substrate (see Theorem 5 below). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L64-L66","doc":"Substrate `ℏ_q = (q - 1) / q`, reused from\n`QBetaCategoricalPrecisionLadder` via `hbarQ'`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.quantumInt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.quantumInt","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MmuR9V9Closure.lean#L60-L62","doc":"Quantum integer `[n]_q = (q^n - q^(-n)) / (q - q^(-1))`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}